    <DataNode elementId="AT5G46240-MONOMER" textLabel="AT5G46240-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q39128" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="O-28, pujar">A cDNA clone was isolated from Arabidopsis thaliana and the gene encoded a single messenger RNA transcript from the Arabidopsis thaliana KAT1 complementary DNA. When recombinantly expressed in Xenopus oocytes, a functional hyperpolarization-activated K+ channel was expressed. The channels encoded by KAT1 are highly selective for K+ over other monovalent cations, are blocked by tetraethylammonium and barium, with typical functional characteristics, of inward-rectifying K+ channels in eukaryotic cells, showing that KAT1 encodes an inward-rectifying K+ channel |CITS: [8966547]|.</Comment>
